# {{project-name}}

Rust application using `che-orm` and the **{{backend}}** backend.
Requires Rust 1.88 or newer. The dependency requires che-orm 0.3.1 or later.

## Run

{% if backend == "postgres" -%}
Create a PostgreSQL database first, then set its connection URL:

```bash
export CHE_ORM_DATABASE_URL='postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost/{{crate_name}}'
```

{% endif -%}
Apply migrations explicitly before running the CRUD demo:

```bash
cargo run --bin manage -- schema
cargo run --bin manage -- migrate
cargo run --bin manage -- migrate status
cargo run
```

The demo creates, reads, saves with `Database::save`, and deletes one task. It does not apply
migrations at startup.

{% if backend == "sqlite" -%}
SQLite uses `app.db` by default. Set `CHE_ORM_DATABASE_URL` to use a different
file. The migration CLI requires a persistent database; tests use in-memory SQLite.
{% else -%}
Without `CHE_ORM_DATABASE_URL`, the default is
`postgresql://localhost/{{crate_name}}`. Authentication and TLS options belong in
your connection settings.
{% endif %}
Exactly one backend feature must be enabled. To switch to the other backend,
disable defaults and enable that feature on **every** command, for example:

```bash
cargo run --no-default-features --features {% if backend == "sqlite" %}postgres{% else %}sqlite{% endif %} --bin manage -- schema
```

## Project layout

- `src/models.rs`: application models.
- `src/lib.rs`: `AppConfig` and application registry.
- `src/settings.rs`: database connection settings.
- `src/migrations/`: compiled migration history and its registry.
- `src/bin/manage.rs`: schema, migration and migration-status commands.
- `src/main.rs`: async CRUD demo.
- `tests/runtime.rs`: schema-history validation and SQLite CRUD coverage.

## Change the schema

The `tasks:0001_initial` migration is frozen independently of the current model.
When changing `Task`, add a new migration module with a new `MigrationId`, its
dependency on the previous migration, and reviewed `MigrationOperation` values.
Register the new module in `src/migrations/mod.rs`.

The schema-history test detects model changes without matching migrations.
Preserve the identities and checksums of applied migrations. Use compiled
migrations for persistent schemas; `create_table` is for tests and local setup.
This CLI does not generate migrations automatically.

## Verify

```bash
cargo fmt --check
cargo test
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
```

With PostgreSQL selected, tests validate the compiled history without connecting
to a server. To also run the in-memory CRUD test, use
`cargo test --no-default-features --features sqlite`. Running PostgreSQL migration
and CRUD commands requires a live database.

See the [che-orm documentation](https://github.com/che4web/che-orm) for relations,
serializers, UUID models and synchronization.
